      ],
      "structuralContentBlocks": 110,
      "canonicalTail": [
        "1. Form a slit $0.5$ mm wide between the jaws of the vernier caliper.",
        "2. Hold the slit vertically close to your eye.",
        "3. Look through the slit at the vertically positioned glowing filament of the lamp. Multicolored fringes (diffraction spectra) appear on both sides of the filament.",
        "4. Increase the slit width from $0.55$ mm to $0.8$ mm and observe the effect on the diffraction spectrum①.",
        "① If a vernier caliper is not available, use a glass photographic plate coated with a black emulsion. Slits of different widths should be scratched in the coating beforehand."
